==English==

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|distinct|-ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈstɪŋktli/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-distinctly.ogg|a=California}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[distinct]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|I '''distinctly''' remember the voice of my deceased grandmother.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Sidereal Messenger of Galileo Galilei and a Part of the Preface to Kepler's Dioptrics Containing the Original Account of Galileo's Astronomical Discoveries: A Translation with Introduction and Notes|year=1880|passage=About ten months ago a report reached my ears that a Dutchman had constructed a telescope, by the aid of which visible objects, although at a great distance from the eye of the observer, were seen '''distinctly''' as if near; {{...}}|author=w:Galileo Galilei|page=10|origdate=13 March 1610|translator=Edward Stafford Carlos|chapter=The Astronomical Messenger|oclc=433105990|publisher=Rivingtons|location=London|author2=w:Johannes Kepler|original=Sidereus Nuncius: {{...}}|type=}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1928|author=Lawrence R. Bourne
|title=Well Tackled!
|chapter=17|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL5387037W
|passage=Commander Birch was a trifle uneasy when he found there was more than a [[popple]] on the sea; it was, in fact, '''distinctly''' choppy.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2007|author=Stephen R. Donaldson|title=Fatal Revenant|page=192|isbn=978-0-399-15446-1|passage="Aloud," he said '''distinctly,''' "the Seven Words are spoken thus. ''Melenkurion abatha. Duroc minas mill. Harad khabaal.''"}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|indistinctly}}

